      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses this high greatly raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
