       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Metformin 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled dose, and you haven't given a clinical reason for exceeding it. Overdosing on metformin can cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis, and I can't think of a situation where this dose would be appropriate for a 70 kg adult.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or 1,700 mg/day split as 850 mg twice daily. If 1,700 mg was meant as the total daily dose, that may be where the mix-up came from.\n- **Help you with an off-label dose.** If you have a specific reason, such as a protocol or a consult recommendation, talk to pharmacy or your attending first. You can then place the order through your hospital's override process.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
